column1:
5:9|Nothing in their mouths is reliable;
within them is destruction.
Their throats are open graves;
their tongues speak smoothly.|Preserves bodily sequence and dangerous flattery.

18:6|In my distress I called on the LORD;
I cried to my God for help.
From his temple he heard my voice;
my cry came before him, into his ears.|Maintain the movement of the cry toward God and the bodily hearing image.
